1
00:00:03,903 --> 00:00:06,333
The baby I had waited for so long,

2
00:00:08,317 --> 00:00:11,447
the baby I considered more precious than my own life,

3
00:00:14,157 --> 00:00:16,427
was suddenly taken from me one day.

4
00:00:19,327 --> 00:00:20,827
I resented the world,

5
00:00:21,327 --> 00:00:22,797
and I resented myself.

6
00:00:24,627 --> 00:00:26,097
I blamed myself...

7
00:00:26,767 --> 00:00:28,297
for failing to protect my baby...

8
00:00:30,237 --> 00:00:32,537
and even attempted to take my own life.

9
00:00:35,907 --> 00:00:36,947
And...

10
00:00:39,147 --> 00:00:40,277
all this time,

11
00:00:43,247 --> 00:00:44,887
in order to protect my husband,

12
00:00:47,357 --> 00:00:50,427
I was going to take this secret to my grave.

13
00:00:53,857 --> 00:00:54,857
But today,

14
00:00:57,027 --> 00:00:58,067
I'm gathering my courage...

15
00:01:01,637 --> 00:01:04,837
to reveal the secret I've kept in my heart...

16
00:01:06,577 --> 00:01:08,237
for the past three years.

17
00:01:11,777 --> 00:01:12,777
I...

18
00:01:17,187 --> 00:01:18,857
took medication that my husband gave me...

19
00:01:20,317 --> 00:01:21,587
and lost my baby.

20
00:01:24,857 --> 00:01:27,857
He gave me medication that I should have never taken.

21
00:01:29,597 --> 00:01:30,697
My husband...

22
00:01:32,297 --> 00:01:34,867
is a murderer who killed our baby.

23
00:01:39,837 --> 00:01:40,837
Plaintiff.

24
00:01:43,347 --> 00:01:45,647
Is what you're saying true?

25
00:01:46,077 --> 00:01:47,817
Yes, it is.

26
00:01:51,887 --> 00:01:53,357
Back when I had my miscarriage,

27
00:01:54,617 --> 00:01:57,257
I confirmed it with my doctor at the time.

28
00:01:58,557 --> 00:02:00,627
I found out that the medication my husband gave me then...

29
00:02:01,557 --> 00:02:03,227
was fatal to the fetus...

30
00:02:03,227 --> 00:02:05,997
What is this bullshit? What do you think you're doing?

31
00:02:06,367 --> 00:02:09,907
Defendant, calm down and take your seat.

32
00:02:16,607 --> 00:02:19,117
Investigator, what she's saying right now...

33
00:02:19,117 --> 00:02:20,777
is completely baseless.

34
00:02:20,877 --> 00:02:22,787
I never gave her any such pills.

35
00:02:22,847 --> 00:02:24,887
More importantly,

36
00:02:24,887 --> 00:02:26,787
why would I ever harm my own child?

37
00:02:26,857 --> 00:02:28,527
This is ridiculous, Investigator.

38
00:02:28,527 --> 00:02:29,927
That's not true, Investigator.

39
00:02:32,827 --> 00:02:36,427
- I'm telling the truth. - Hey!

40
00:02:36,497 --> 00:02:37,827
Quiet, please.

41
00:02:43,507 --> 00:02:46,837
We won't be able to continue the investigation today.

42
00:02:47,237 --> 00:02:49,177
We'll reconvene at the next hearing.

43
00:02:52,247 --> 00:02:53,277
Hey, are you out of your mind?

44
00:02:53,717 --> 00:02:55,117
You're supposed to just state the facts,

45
00:02:55,177 --> 00:02:57,217
so why are you making up this insane story?

46
00:02:57,287 --> 00:02:58,287
It's not a story.

47
00:02:59,057 --> 00:03:01,717
Why would I come all this way just to make things up?

48
00:03:01,887 --> 00:03:04,087
What kind of pills are you even saying I gave you?

49
00:03:04,357 --> 00:03:05,527
Do you really not remember?

50
00:03:06,127 --> 00:03:07,557
Pills or whatever else,

51
00:03:07,627 --> 00:03:10,367
I never gave you anything that could have harmed you.

52
00:03:10,767 --> 00:03:13,997
Then maybe you should take this chance to think hard.

53
00:03:15,097 --> 00:03:17,937
Think about if you've only ever given me good things,

54
00:03:17,937 --> 00:03:18,937
pills or otherwise.

55
00:03:19,437 --> 00:03:20,537
Unbelievable.

56
00:03:20,837 --> 00:03:23,007
(Yeonnam Family Court Bulletin)

57
00:03:23,447 --> 00:03:24,447
Fine.

58
00:03:24,507 --> 00:03:27,117
Let's just say you're having some ridiculous delusion for now.

59
00:03:27,747 --> 00:03:29,317
Then why have you been quiet all this time?

60
00:03:29,917 --> 00:03:33,257
Why say nothing until now and then cause a scene here?

61
00:03:34,557 --> 00:03:35,757
I was going to...

62
00:03:37,457 --> 00:03:39,127
just carry this burden alone.

63
00:03:40,957 --> 00:03:42,567
I was worried it would be too hard on you.

64
00:03:43,627 --> 00:03:45,537
- But... - But what?

65
00:03:48,067 --> 00:03:49,107
What?

66
00:03:49,407 --> 00:03:51,007
I just don't want to anymore.

67
00:03:52,937 --> 00:03:56,247
I can't wait to see what you'll do to me now.

68
00:03:57,047 --> 00:04:01,877
After all, you were so worried when Hee Ju just took some pills.

69
00:04:08,487 --> 00:04:09,487
Gosh.

70
00:04:12,097 --> 00:04:13,157
Do you really not remember?

71
00:04:16,667 --> 00:04:17,767
(Episode 8)

72
00:04:20,097 --> 00:04:21,967
If what your wife is saying is true,

73
00:04:22,807 --> 00:04:24,507
this is incredibly serious.

74
00:04:25,167 --> 00:04:28,607
My wife said she even got a written statement from her doctor.

75
00:04:29,177 --> 00:04:32,077
But I don't even remember buying any pills myself.

76
00:04:32,247 --> 00:04:34,877
Then you should have asked your wife for more details.

77
00:04:34,977 --> 00:04:37,247
This isn't something you can just ignore.

78
00:04:37,647 --> 00:04:40,387
This is separate from the divorce lawsuit.

79
00:04:40,757 --> 00:04:42,357
This could easily be considered attempted murder.

80
00:04:42,787 --> 00:04:44,127
Attempted murder?

81
00:04:44,687 --> 00:04:46,257
No, then does that mean...

82
00:04:46,327 --> 00:04:49,067
when my wife attacked me with a knife...

83
00:04:49,127 --> 00:04:50,967
It's certainly possible.

84
00:04:51,067 --> 00:04:52,297
If she believes the baby died...

85
00:04:52,367 --> 00:04:53,967
because of the pills you gave her,

86
00:04:54,037 --> 00:04:57,267
she would have been much more emotionally unstable and sensitive.

87
00:04:57,437 --> 00:05:00,237
Well, I'm emotionally unstable too.

88
00:05:00,637 --> 00:05:03,077
I have no idea when or where she'll drop another bombshell,

89
00:05:03,077 --> 00:05:06,017
so my heart is pounding, and I feel like I'm going crazy.

90
00:05:06,647 --> 00:05:09,587
Is that why you were so nervous about your secret relationship...

91
00:05:09,587 --> 00:05:10,887
that you made her sign a written pledge?

92
00:05:11,517 --> 00:05:13,987
How did we get back to talking about that?

93
00:05:14,617 --> 00:05:18,187
Anyway, look into it. If there was a mistake, correct it.

94
00:05:19,097 --> 00:05:20,097
Okay.

95
00:05:21,757 --> 00:05:23,397
And you should probably break up with your girlfriend.

96
00:05:24,127 --> 00:05:25,127
What?

97
00:05:25,997 --> 00:05:28,467
Are you just going to continue this loving relationship?

98
00:05:28,667 --> 00:05:30,567
She's the reason this bombshell dropped in the first place.

99
00:05:32,237 --> 00:05:33,507
Oh, honestly.

100
00:05:45,717 --> 00:05:47,017
Good morning.

101
00:05:48,357 --> 00:05:51,457
Why the long faces? You look like you've seen a ghost.

102
00:05:51,827 --> 00:05:53,757
Don't you have a job?

103
00:05:54,057 --> 00:05:56,067
I mean, you seem pretty free for a weekday morning.

104
00:05:57,767 --> 00:05:59,437
I'm a freelancer.

105
00:05:59,837 --> 00:06:01,197
I take days off when I don't have work.

106
00:06:01,637 --> 00:06:04,137
Today is one of those days.

107
00:06:06,407 --> 00:06:08,307
Oh, can I see your phone for a second?

108
00:06:08,637 --> 00:06:10,577
- What? - Quickly.

109
00:06:13,447 --> 00:06:16,587
My name is Ahn Hee Ju.

110
00:06:17,087 --> 00:06:18,217
Not "miss."

111
00:06:19,857 --> 00:06:22,087
You should save my number, just in case.

112
00:06:22,327 --> 00:06:24,187
So you don't break down my door for no reason.

113
00:06:24,487 --> 00:06:26,897
So her last name is Ahn. Ahn Hee Ju.

114
00:06:26,957 --> 00:06:29,397
Oh, honestly. Why are you saving her number?

115
00:06:31,127 --> 00:06:34,237
I'm not going to argue. Get out of this house today.

116
00:06:34,367 --> 00:06:36,907
I'll give you a full refund for the month's rent.

117
00:06:37,037 --> 00:06:39,007
Mom, that's a huge loss for us.

118
00:06:39,107 --> 00:06:40,437
If I get sick from the stress she's causing me,

119
00:06:40,507 --> 00:06:41,507
that'll be an even bigger loss.

120
00:06:42,307 --> 00:06:43,777
You'll be out by the end of the day, right?

121
00:06:44,377 --> 00:06:46,247
- No. - What?

122
00:06:46,917 --> 00:06:50,747
Mother, please don't hate me so much.

123
00:06:51,217 --> 00:06:53,417
You're CEO Ji's mother,

124
00:06:53,417 --> 00:06:55,117
so I'd really like for us to get along.

125
00:06:55,187 --> 00:06:56,187
What?

126
00:06:56,857 --> 00:06:59,197
How dare you call me Mother?

127
00:06:59,357 --> 00:07:01,157
You don't like it?

128
00:07:01,797 --> 00:07:04,267
Then I'll just call you Grandma.

129
00:07:04,467 --> 00:07:06,037
I'm more comfortable with that, actually.

130
00:07:06,897 --> 00:07:07,967
Grandma.

131
00:07:09,337 --> 00:07:10,837
Well, I'll be heading up then.

132
00:07:15,907 --> 00:07:16,947
Grandma?

133
00:07:18,977 --> 00:07:20,117
Mom, you are a grandma.

134
00:07:20,517 --> 00:07:21,517
Hey, you little brat.

135
00:07:41,067 --> 00:07:43,367
This...

136
00:07:43,437 --> 00:07:45,737
If it has two lines, you're pregnant, right?

137
00:07:45,977 --> 00:07:47,937
Are you pregnant? You're pregnant?

138
00:07:50,377 --> 00:07:51,577
I'm going to be a dad!

139
00:07:51,577 --> 00:07:53,817
Mi Young, you've been through so much.

140
00:07:53,817 --> 00:07:55,787
The baby I had waited for so long,

141
00:07:57,787 --> 00:08:00,757
the baby I considered more precious than my own life,

142
00:08:03,587 --> 00:08:05,827
was suddenly taken from me one day.

143
00:08:10,067 --> 00:08:11,067
I...

144
00:08:12,897 --> 00:08:14,967
took medication that my husband gave me...

145
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:17,267
and lost my baby.

146
00:08:19,107 --> 00:08:22,647
He gave me medication that I should have never taken.

147
00:08:24,607 --> 00:08:25,777
My husband...

148
00:08:26,977 --> 00:08:29,487
is a murderer who killed our baby.

149
00:08:42,697 --> 00:08:44,597
Are you sure you aren't mistaken?

150
00:08:44,997 --> 00:08:47,237
I already had the drug's components analysed.

151
00:08:47,797 --> 00:08:49,537
That medication was the direct cause...

152
00:08:50,167 --> 00:08:51,237
of my miscarriage.

153
00:08:55,107 --> 00:08:57,577
Still, how could pills cause a miscarriage?

154
00:08:57,977 --> 00:09:01,247
I'm sure those pills were meant to be good for you.

155
00:09:01,517 --> 00:09:04,287
That's right. Pill that were meant to be good for me.

156
00:09:05,117 --> 00:09:06,117
But...

157
00:09:07,117 --> 00:09:09,887
it was something a pregnant woman should never take.

158
00:09:14,357 --> 00:09:15,567
Wait.

159
00:09:16,597 --> 00:09:19,297
When did you start taking those pills?

160
00:09:20,037 --> 00:09:21,097
Let's see.

161
00:09:21,837 --> 00:09:26,507
Ji Won Ho gave me the pills around Chuseok,

162
00:09:27,577 --> 00:09:29,307
so I must have taken it for at least two months.

163
00:09:30,607 --> 00:09:31,647
Around Chuseok?

164
00:09:32,007 --> 00:09:33,847
We were sponsoring a group wedding then,

165
00:09:33,847 --> 00:09:35,787
so I was completely swamped.

166
00:09:36,217 --> 00:09:38,047
So even if I skipped meals,

167
00:09:38,047 --> 00:09:40,287
I made sure to take the pills without fail.

168
00:09:42,687 --> 00:09:44,057
Taking those pills...

169
00:09:45,927 --> 00:09:49,427
is the biggest regret of my life.

170
00:09:59,877 --> 00:10:00,877
What?

171
00:10:01,277 --> 00:10:02,407
What's with that look on your face?

172
00:10:03,207 --> 00:10:04,207
What?

173
00:10:05,207 --> 00:10:06,247
It's nothing.

174
00:10:10,317 --> 00:10:12,757
Anyway, you must have gone through so much.

175
00:10:13,957 --> 00:10:14,957
To be honest,

176
00:10:15,787 --> 00:10:16,927
I'm still struggling.

177
00:10:19,157 --> 00:10:20,527
Even as time passes,

178
00:10:21,327 --> 00:10:22,897
I can't seem to forget.

179
00:10:26,853 --> 00:10:27,883
Gosh.

180
00:10:30,653 --> 00:10:32,823
Oh, my lawyer's here. I'm going to head up first.

181
00:10:32,893 --> 00:10:34,593
Okay. Hope it goes well.

182
00:10:34,853 --> 00:10:36,563
- Can you clean this up? - Of course.

183
00:10:36,563 --> 00:10:37,623
- Sorry. - It's okay.

184
00:10:42,137 --> 00:10:43,707
So that's what happened?

185
00:10:44,507 --> 00:10:45,577
But wait...

186
00:10:46,777 --> 00:10:48,917
Why didn't you tell me this before?

187
00:10:49,447 --> 00:10:51,847
- Pardon? - If it was something this serious,

188
00:10:52,047 --> 00:10:54,787
we wouldn't have had to be so roundabout.

189
00:10:56,627 --> 00:10:58,357
Are you sure it was your husband's mistake?

190
00:10:58,787 --> 00:11:00,857
If there's any evidence he gave you it intentionally...

191
00:11:00,927 --> 00:11:02,297
Absolutely not.

192
00:11:03,497 --> 00:11:04,727
My husband...

193
00:11:05,327 --> 00:11:08,237
wanted a child as desperately as I did.

194
00:11:09,507 --> 00:11:11,937
He had no reason to do something like that to me on purpose.

195
00:11:13,007 --> 00:11:14,737
But if that's the case,

196
00:11:15,877 --> 00:11:17,047
doesn't that make it even stranger?

197
00:11:19,047 --> 00:11:23,587
If your husband wanted to give you medication meant only for you,

198
00:11:24,347 --> 00:11:26,617
he would have simply asked for that when he bought it.

199
00:11:27,357 --> 00:11:28,357
That's true.

200
00:11:28,787 --> 00:11:30,257
When my husband bought the medication...

201
00:11:30,327 --> 00:11:33,427
He should have asked for medication for a pregnant woman.

202
00:11:34,427 --> 00:11:35,997
But what you took...

203
00:11:36,527 --> 00:11:39,337
was something fatal for pregnant women.

204
00:11:40,167 --> 00:11:43,537
I just thought my husband was being careless.

205
00:11:43,907 --> 00:11:45,767
During the delivery process,

206
00:11:46,837 --> 00:11:48,777
don't you think there could have been a mix-up?

207
00:11:49,177 --> 00:11:50,377
A mix-up?

208
00:11:56,747 --> 00:11:59,457
There's no way you'd give your wife pills like that.

209
00:12:00,657 --> 00:12:03,187
To win the lawsuit, don't you think she's going too far?

210
00:12:03,757 --> 00:12:04,957
But then again, Mi Young...

211
00:12:04,957 --> 00:12:07,197
isn't the type to make something like that up.

212
00:12:10,797 --> 00:12:11,797
Wait a minute.

213
00:12:12,227 --> 00:12:13,997
Did you think of something?

214
00:12:16,667 --> 00:12:17,907
Could it be that?

215
00:12:20,077 --> 00:12:22,907
It'd be such a waste to send this back.

216
00:12:24,877 --> 00:12:26,747
If I were to buy this,

217
00:12:26,977 --> 00:12:29,247
it would easily cost several hundred dollars.

218
00:12:31,087 --> 00:12:32,817
What's so expensive?

219
00:12:33,987 --> 00:12:35,057
Oh, it's just...

220
00:12:35,757 --> 00:12:38,987
a holiday gift that came to the office for Chuseok.

221
00:12:39,557 --> 00:12:42,567
CEO Baek told me to return any gifts...

222
00:12:42,667 --> 00:12:44,927
that might be considered a bribe without a second thought.

223
00:12:45,467 --> 00:12:46,767
Then just send it back.

224
00:12:46,937 --> 00:12:48,667
What if something goes wrong because you accepted it?

225
00:12:49,067 --> 00:12:51,937
But with this one, it's a little unclear...

226
00:12:52,007 --> 00:12:54,307
if it's a bribe or not.

227
00:12:54,437 --> 00:12:55,637
Where's it from?

228
00:12:56,977 --> 00:13:00,677
Well, from some place with a lot of money.

229
00:13:01,147 --> 00:13:02,947
A wealthy company that's so rich...

230
00:13:03,017 --> 00:13:05,447
that they wouldn't even notice giving away something like this.

231
00:13:06,357 --> 00:13:07,357
Is that so?

232
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:08,787
Look,

233
00:13:09,017 --> 00:13:12,597
CEO Ji, from the looks of it, these are very expensive pills.

234
00:13:13,157 --> 00:13:15,697
Just one pill will give you a huge boost of energy.

235
00:13:16,227 --> 00:13:17,397
A huge boost of energy?

236
00:13:17,597 --> 00:13:18,597
Yes.

237
00:13:21,097 --> 00:13:22,437
Should we...

238
00:13:23,037 --> 00:13:24,337
give this to Mi Young?

239
00:13:25,037 --> 00:13:26,077
Mi Young?

240
00:13:26,077 --> 00:13:29,447
She's had morning sickness lately and hasn't been able to eat well.

241
00:13:29,507 --> 00:13:31,547
It would be good for her to take something like this.

242
00:13:33,017 --> 00:13:35,417
Mi Young will be angry if she finds out.

243
00:13:36,617 --> 00:13:38,087
That's why...

244
00:13:38,517 --> 00:13:40,787
you shouldn't say it's from a client.

245
00:13:41,357 --> 00:13:43,757
Just say you bought it.

246
00:13:44,457 --> 00:13:47,157
- What do you think? - You gave that to Mi Young?

247
00:13:47,897 --> 00:13:49,197
Yes.

248
00:13:49,367 --> 00:13:51,127
I gave it to her as if I bought it.

249
00:13:51,367 --> 00:13:53,337
Did you even check what kind of pills they were?

250
00:13:54,497 --> 00:13:57,237
I just heard A Ri say it was expensive and good.

251
00:13:57,367 --> 00:13:58,637
But she was pregnant.

252
00:13:58,707 --> 00:14:01,037
You should have checked the ingredients carefully.

253
00:14:01,637 --> 00:14:04,247
Or you should have just been honest and told her it was a gift.

254
00:14:04,847 --> 00:14:06,617
Why did you pretend you bought it?

255
00:14:06,817 --> 00:14:09,417
You know how it is. When women are pregnant,

256
00:14:09,487 --> 00:14:10,817
they want their husbands to be attentive...

257
00:14:10,887 --> 00:14:12,517
and show they care.

258
00:14:12,787 --> 00:14:14,057
I just thought if I said I bought it,

259
00:14:14,117 --> 00:14:15,657
she'd be happier.

260
00:14:16,087 --> 00:14:17,487
You tried to take credit for something free,

261
00:14:17,757 --> 00:14:18,987
and look what happened.

262
00:14:19,427 --> 00:14:21,627
But I'm sure it's not that kind of pill.

263
00:14:23,767 --> 00:14:26,237
I shouldn't be sitting here. I should just go ask A Ri.

264
00:14:26,237 --> 00:14:27,367
Hey, wait a minute.

265
00:14:30,167 --> 00:14:32,307
If it really is because of the pills from Director Song,

266
00:14:32,877 --> 00:14:33,937
what will happen?

267
00:14:34,407 --> 00:14:35,437
What?

268
00:14:35,437 --> 00:14:38,307
If she finds out her best friend had a miscarriage because of her,

269
00:14:39,547 --> 00:14:40,547
do you think...

270
00:14:41,217 --> 00:14:42,277
Director Song will be okay?

271
00:14:43,647 --> 00:14:45,517
Of course she won't.

272
00:14:46,317 --> 00:14:48,517
I know it's not my place to get involved in your marriage,

273
00:14:49,727 --> 00:14:51,427
but you really need to think this through.

274
00:14:52,157 --> 00:14:53,927
I'm talking about this constant emotional fighting,

275
00:14:54,227 --> 00:14:56,067
always bringing up the past.

276
00:14:57,397 --> 00:14:59,167
What happened with the baby is truly tragic,

277
00:14:59,567 --> 00:15:03,367
but losing Director Song over this doesn't seem right.

278
00:15:04,407 --> 00:15:05,967
Still, I have to check.

279
00:15:06,037 --> 00:15:08,237
It might turn out to have nothing to do with A Ri.

280
00:15:08,337 --> 00:15:09,347
Given the circumstances,

281
00:15:09,407 --> 00:15:10,977
it's obvious it was Director Song's mistake.

282
00:15:11,047 --> 00:15:13,647
Okay. I understand what you're saying.

283
00:15:14,177 --> 00:15:16,087
I'll find the right time to bring this up with her.

284
00:15:16,287 --> 00:15:17,687
I'll try not to shock A Ri too much.

285
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:26,857
(Calvin Care Holdings, Nutritional Facts And Directions)

286
00:15:31,527 --> 00:15:32,837
(Supplements Unsafe for Pregnant Women)

287
00:15:36,807 --> 00:15:37,807
Director Song.

288
00:15:39,307 --> 00:15:40,407
Yes, Vice President Kang.

289
00:15:40,877 --> 00:15:41,877
Are you okay?

290
00:15:42,177 --> 00:15:43,177
Yes?

291
00:15:44,247 --> 00:15:45,277
What about?

292
00:15:46,417 --> 00:15:47,417
It's nothing.

293
00:15:48,247 --> 00:15:50,387
By the way, did you place the fabric order?

294
00:15:51,187 --> 00:15:52,417
Oh, right.

295
00:15:53,017 --> 00:15:54,787
I was supposed to place the order today.

296
00:15:55,417 --> 00:15:57,787
I'm sorry. I forgot.

297
00:15:59,027 --> 00:16:00,497
Please have it done this morning.

298
00:16:01,227 --> 00:16:03,027
Yes, I'll place the order right away.

299
00:16:21,577 --> 00:16:23,747
(Jihwaja Motel)

300
00:16:26,657 --> 00:16:28,787
I can't just kick that troublemaker out.

301
00:16:29,157 --> 00:16:30,187
What am I going to do?

302
00:16:30,557 --> 00:16:32,827
Couldn't we just ignore her for now?

303
00:16:33,057 --> 00:16:35,197
But if we do that, who knows what trouble she'll stir up.

304
00:16:35,797 --> 00:16:36,797
That's true.

305
00:16:37,497 --> 00:16:39,067
The thought alone is terrifying.

306
00:16:40,137 --> 00:16:43,367
Mom, what if we start some smoke in front of her room?

307
00:16:43,607 --> 00:16:44,607
What?

308
00:16:44,667 --> 00:16:46,907
If she thinks there's a fire, she'll come running out, right?

309
00:16:47,037 --> 00:16:48,537
Are you trying to burn the house down...

310
00:16:48,537 --> 00:16:49,607
to get rid of a mouse?

311
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:54,177
But that girl looks so normal.

312
00:16:54,277 --> 00:16:55,677
I don't get what she sees in Won Ho.

313
00:16:55,777 --> 00:16:57,087
What's not to like?

314
00:16:57,247 --> 00:17:01,217
Won Ho is handsome and capable. He's second to none.

315
00:17:01,517 --> 00:17:02,927
Even after he breaks up with that fox,

316
00:17:02,987 --> 00:17:04,857
he could get remarried two more times.

317
00:17:05,127 --> 00:17:07,027
Still, two more times is a bit...

318
00:17:09,097 --> 00:17:10,097
Mom.

319
00:17:10,467 --> 00:17:12,727
- That's it. - What?

320
00:17:12,967 --> 00:17:14,897
You're not the first.

321
00:17:15,297 --> 00:17:17,067
The one before you was in Room 203.

322
00:17:17,707 --> 00:17:19,507
The one before her was in Room 403.

323
00:17:19,707 --> 00:17:22,477
Plenty have already come and gone. Women who liked Won Ho.

324
00:17:22,807 --> 00:17:24,707
To him, you're just one of those women,

325
00:17:24,707 --> 00:17:25,807
one who is just passing through.

326
00:17:26,377 --> 00:17:28,247
The only woman who will be with Won Ho until the end...

327
00:17:28,417 --> 00:17:29,717
is my sister-in-law.

328
00:17:35,087 --> 00:17:36,357
Was what I said that funny?

329
00:17:38,327 --> 00:17:40,897
No. It's just so ridiculous.

330
00:17:41,697 --> 00:17:43,797
- What? - It is ridiculous.

331
00:17:44,127 --> 00:17:47,497
Making up a story like that just to get rid of me.

332
00:17:47,597 --> 00:17:49,337
I'm telling you, it's the truth.

333
00:17:49,637 --> 00:17:51,137
Don't waste your breath.

334
00:17:51,567 --> 00:17:53,477
I don't care if a truckload of women have come and gone.

335
00:17:53,637 --> 00:17:55,307
There's no way I'm leaving.

336
00:17:55,607 --> 00:17:57,147
What do you like so much about Won Ho?

337
00:17:57,907 --> 00:17:58,907
It's just...

338
00:17:59,747 --> 00:18:00,817
destiny.

339
00:18:00,877 --> 00:18:02,947
- What? - I knew the moment I saw him...

340
00:18:03,247 --> 00:18:06,687
that CEO Ji is the man of my destiny.

341
00:18:06,887 --> 00:18:09,457
That's enough. If you keep this up...

342
00:18:09,527 --> 00:18:11,827
You're the one who needs to stop.

343
00:18:12,087 --> 00:18:13,397
When I lose my temper,

344
00:18:14,497 --> 00:18:15,727
I get really nasty.

345
00:18:16,267 --> 00:18:18,297
So what if you get nasty?

346
00:18:18,867 --> 00:18:20,537
Are you going to hurt me or something?

347
00:18:22,367 --> 00:18:23,367
That's right.

348
00:18:24,207 --> 00:18:26,677
I should take care of that guy first.

349
00:18:31,147 --> 00:18:32,947
Yes, is this the customer service center...

350
00:18:32,947 --> 00:18:34,877
for the pharmaceutical company?

351
00:18:35,747 --> 00:18:38,947
I'm calling because I have a question about a supplement.

352
00:18:39,687 --> 00:18:40,687
Yes.

353
00:18:41,487 --> 00:18:44,157
The specific supplement is...

354
00:18:44,927 --> 00:18:46,057
Director Song.

355
00:18:46,997 --> 00:18:48,997
Yes, I'll have to call you back.

356
00:18:50,427 --> 00:18:52,897
Oh, Young Yun, what is it?

357
00:18:53,067 --> 00:18:54,097
Director Song,

358
00:18:54,297 --> 00:18:56,667
you should get to the office right away.

359
00:18:57,667 --> 00:18:59,207
How could you make such a huge mistake?

360
00:18:59,637 --> 00:19:02,307
How could you accidentally add an extra zero?

361
00:19:02,807 --> 00:19:04,577
It's a good thing I checked.

362
00:19:04,807 --> 00:19:06,347
What would have happened if the order had gone through...

363
00:19:06,347 --> 00:19:07,347
like that?

364
00:19:08,117 --> 00:19:09,147
I'm so sorry.

365
00:19:09,477 --> 00:19:10,517
I'm so sorry.

366
00:19:10,747 --> 00:19:14,117
Director Song. Where on earth is your head at?

367
00:19:16,927 --> 00:19:17,927
Vice President Kang.

368
00:19:18,757 --> 00:19:20,357
Let's leave it at that.

369
00:19:21,227 --> 00:19:23,467
Besides, it's been handled, thankfully.

370
00:19:29,707 --> 00:19:30,837
Also,

371
00:19:31,707 --> 00:19:32,737
I think Director Song...

372
00:19:33,377 --> 00:19:36,207
- knows it was her mistake. - What?

373
00:19:36,407 --> 00:19:39,477
- A Ri knows already? How? - Mi Young must have told her.

374
00:19:40,247 --> 00:19:42,817
I saw a search history for supplements...

375
00:19:44,187 --> 00:19:46,417
on Director Song's computer earlier.

376
00:19:48,287 --> 00:19:50,857
Supplements that pregnant women shouldn't take.

377
00:20:12,877 --> 00:20:14,577
Hey. What's going on?

378
00:20:15,877 --> 00:20:18,447
Oh, that place? Yes, I like it too.

379
00:20:19,817 --> 00:20:20,817
Should we?

380
00:20:21,417 --> 00:20:22,417
What time?

381
00:20:24,527 --> 00:20:26,127
Okay, sounds good.

382
00:20:26,957 --> 00:20:29,027
The reservation is under Calvin, right?

383
00:20:30,627 --> 00:20:32,027
Okay, see you later.

384
00:20:35,067 --> 00:20:36,407
You scared me.

385
00:20:37,267 --> 00:20:39,037
Gosh, you came in so quietly.

386
00:20:39,107 --> 00:20:40,477
Why are you so surprised?

387
00:20:40,677 --> 00:20:42,437
Do I have to kick the door in for you to hear me?

388
00:20:42,837 --> 00:20:44,547
What, do you have something to say?

389
00:20:44,947 --> 00:20:46,977
You seem to be pretty close with Calvin these days.

390
00:20:47,677 --> 00:20:50,747
- What? - Looks like you're off somewhere.

391
00:20:50,817 --> 00:20:51,987
What's it to you?

392
00:20:52,487 --> 00:20:54,987
Says one half of the inseparable Couple of the Century.

393
00:20:56,117 --> 00:20:57,157
"Couple of the Century?"

394
00:20:57,657 --> 00:20:58,927
Hey, I need to get back to work.

395
00:20:58,987 --> 00:21:00,227
If you have something to say, say it and leave.

396
00:21:03,327 --> 00:21:04,667
If something...

397
00:21:06,197 --> 00:21:08,037
really went wrong because of those pills,

398
00:21:10,307 --> 00:21:11,967
could you forgive the person who gave it to you?

399
00:21:13,007 --> 00:21:14,007
What?

400
00:21:14,007 --> 00:21:17,007
I'm saying, if it wasn't me but someone else,

401
00:21:18,347 --> 00:21:19,877
could you forgive that person?

402
00:21:21,747 --> 00:21:22,747
First of all,

403
00:21:24,617 --> 00:21:25,817
I took that supplement,

404
00:21:26,987 --> 00:21:28,317
and something happened to our baby.

405
00:21:29,557 --> 00:21:30,957
That is an unchangeable fact.

406
00:21:32,287 --> 00:21:33,297
And...

407
00:21:34,427 --> 00:21:36,057
would I be able to forgive the person...

408
00:21:36,467 --> 00:21:38,527
who gave me the wrong pills if it wasn't you?

409
00:21:40,797 --> 00:21:41,797
No.

410
00:21:43,767 --> 00:21:45,607
The only reason I put up with it was because it was you.

411
00:21:47,837 --> 00:21:50,507
The only way I could endure it for three years...

412
00:21:53,577 --> 00:21:56,787
was because the person who gave me that supplement wasn't a stranger.

413
00:21:58,917 --> 00:22:00,687
It was because it was you.

414
00:22:10,427 --> 00:22:12,427
(Conference Room)

415
00:22:23,077 --> 00:22:24,077
I...

416
00:22:26,247 --> 00:22:27,877
took medication that my husband gave me...

417
00:22:29,317 --> 00:22:30,647
and lost my baby.

418
00:22:40,997 --> 00:22:44,097
CEO Ji, I have something urgent to tell you.

419
00:22:44,597 --> 00:22:46,597
I'll be waiting at the cafe up ahead.

420
00:22:53,337 --> 00:22:54,337
CEO Ji.

421
00:22:56,207 --> 00:22:59,707
The reason I asked to see you out here is...

422
00:22:59,847 --> 00:23:02,177
Well, I mean, it's not that...

423
00:23:04,317 --> 00:23:06,217
You heard from Mi Young, right?

424
00:23:09,287 --> 00:23:10,357
About the pills...

425
00:23:11,257 --> 00:23:12,257
Yes.

426
00:23:12,927 --> 00:23:13,997
I heard.

427
00:23:19,967 --> 00:23:23,167
Still, thank you. I wasn't sure how to bring it up,

428
00:23:23,537 --> 00:23:24,767
so I was really hesitant.

429
00:23:26,067 --> 00:23:27,777
So thank you for being brave enough to do it first.

430
00:23:28,007 --> 00:23:29,437
But I really...

431
00:23:30,247 --> 00:23:32,307
didn't think it would be a problem.

432
00:23:34,477 --> 00:23:35,917
I know.

433
00:23:38,817 --> 00:23:40,057
You're not a pharmacist, A Ri.

434
00:23:40,117 --> 00:23:42,517
How could you possibly know all of the ingredients?

435
00:23:43,557 --> 00:23:44,557
It was just...

436
00:23:45,857 --> 00:23:47,327
really bad luck.

437
00:23:48,327 --> 00:23:51,727
Unfortunately, those pills were very harmful to pregnant women.

438
00:23:53,437 --> 00:23:54,797
That's not it.

439
00:23:56,807 --> 00:23:57,867
It's not?

440
00:23:58,237 --> 00:24:02,437
It was just a simple health supplement.

441
00:24:02,637 --> 00:24:04,807
It was packed with all sorts of healthy ingredients.

442
00:24:05,447 --> 00:24:08,517
I called the pharmaceutical company earlier and confirmed everything.

443
00:24:08,717 --> 00:24:09,847
Oh, really?

444
00:24:11,387 --> 00:24:13,517
Right. I knew it.

445
00:24:13,587 --> 00:24:16,487
No wonder. That didn't make any sense.

446
00:24:18,787 --> 00:24:21,397
Oh, A Ri, I'm sorry. I guess I jumped to conclusions.

447
00:24:21,457 --> 00:24:23,427
I'm so sorry. I mean...

448
00:24:23,767 --> 00:24:24,867
Oh, thank you.

449
00:24:26,697 --> 00:24:28,337
No...

450
00:24:29,597 --> 00:24:31,007
It's my fault.

451
00:24:32,767 --> 00:24:34,037
How is it your fault, A Ri?

452
00:24:34,107 --> 00:24:36,107
You said there was nothing wrong with the pills, right?

453
00:24:36,177 --> 00:24:38,777
There's nothing wrong with those pills.

454
00:24:39,877 --> 00:24:42,317
But the person who gave them to me...

455
00:24:44,917 --> 00:24:46,587
was Calvin.

456
00:24:48,017 --> 00:24:49,017
What?

457
00:24:49,357 --> 00:24:50,627
Back then,

458
00:24:51,827 --> 00:24:53,497
the person who sent the pills...

459
00:24:54,227 --> 00:24:55,957
was Calvin.

460
00:25:08,177 --> 00:25:09,977
When I checked the package,

461
00:25:10,147 --> 00:25:12,707
the sender was Calvin.

462
00:25:13,207 --> 00:25:15,717
I knew Mi Young would be furious if she found out,

463
00:25:15,977 --> 00:25:18,347
but since Calvin was the one who sent it,

464
00:25:18,447 --> 00:25:19,847
I just assumed it had to be something good.

465
00:25:19,917 --> 00:25:22,357
That's what I thought. That's why, but...

466
00:25:23,587 --> 00:25:24,657
If...

467
00:25:25,927 --> 00:25:27,397
Calvin...

468
00:25:28,497 --> 00:25:31,367
tampered with those pills somehow...

469
00:25:35,337 --> 00:25:36,497
Three years ago,

470
00:25:37,437 --> 00:25:41,237
the day the detailed test results came back negative for paternity,

471
00:25:41,807 --> 00:25:44,177
I happened to see Mi Young at the hospital.

472
00:25:45,707 --> 00:25:47,947
She looked pregnant.

473
00:25:51,447 --> 00:25:53,557
I couldn't bring myself to say hello,

474
00:25:53,917 --> 00:25:55,817
and just watched her from a distance.

475
00:25:56,987 --> 00:25:58,787
Seeing Mi Young pregnant...

476
00:25:59,627 --> 00:26:01,157
gave me a strange feeling.

477
00:26:03,827 --> 00:26:05,567
It was a bitter feeling.

478
00:26:20,947 --> 00:26:22,047
I thought we...

479
00:26:22,477 --> 00:26:24,347
were done with each other.

480
00:26:24,747 --> 00:26:26,647
We might have been.

481
00:26:27,217 --> 00:26:29,217
If you hadn't done what you did to me.

482
00:26:29,917 --> 00:26:30,987
What I did?

483
00:26:31,087 --> 00:26:32,487
You ordered it, didn't you?

484
00:26:33,157 --> 00:26:34,497
Having me pushed off the cliff.

485
00:26:34,857 --> 00:26:37,967
Are you still angry about being pushed off a cliff?

486
00:26:38,567 --> 00:26:41,737
- What? - You fell off a cliff,

487
00:26:41,837 --> 00:26:43,537
and you're completely fine.

488
00:26:44,307 --> 00:26:46,007
If I were you, I'd be grateful.

489
00:26:48,477 --> 00:26:50,807
Like I'd been given a new lease on life.

490
00:26:51,207 --> 00:26:52,807
Maybe I'd want to live differently than before...

491
00:26:53,147 --> 00:26:55,417
and be a better person.

492
00:26:57,347 --> 00:26:58,647
Are you messing with me?

493
00:27:00,417 --> 00:27:01,987
I will get my revenge.

494
00:27:03,087 --> 00:27:06,797
What you did to me, I'm going to do the same to you.

495
00:27:10,967 --> 00:27:11,967
Go on.

496
00:27:12,267 --> 00:27:13,537
You're welcome to try anytime.

497
00:27:14,437 --> 00:27:15,837
But before you do,

498
00:27:16,197 --> 00:27:17,437
bring me proof.

499
00:27:18,067 --> 00:27:19,067
What?

500
00:27:19,137 --> 00:27:21,537
Proof that I pushed you off the cliff.

501
00:27:22,707 --> 00:27:24,207
Whether it's revenge or something else,

502
00:27:24,507 --> 00:27:26,917
shouldn't you get your facts straight first?

503
00:27:35,287 --> 00:27:38,127
- Yes. - Sir, you have a visitor.

504
00:27:38,357 --> 00:27:40,497
- Where is Calvin right now? - You can't go in right now.

505
00:27:40,557 --> 00:27:43,157
- Is he here? I just need a minute. - Please wait, sir.

506
00:27:44,197 --> 00:27:45,327
CEO Ji.

507
00:27:46,467 --> 00:27:47,997
What brings you here so suddenly at this hour?

508
00:27:48,097 --> 00:27:50,437
Something just came up that I need to ask you.

509
00:27:50,707 --> 00:27:52,507
You're here to confront something too?

510
00:27:52,507 --> 00:27:53,877
Stay out of this.

511
00:27:56,907 --> 00:27:58,377
I said, get out.

512
00:27:59,447 --> 00:28:00,447
Okay.

513
00:28:09,387 --> 00:28:11,627
(Hotel Calvin)

514
00:28:12,387 --> 00:28:15,127
What is it you want to know? Go ahead and ask.

515
00:28:15,527 --> 00:28:16,697
Do you remember...

516
00:28:17,527 --> 00:28:19,727
the supplement you sent to Mi Young three years ago?

517
00:28:20,027 --> 00:28:23,537
Are you referring to the holiday gift our company sends...

518
00:28:24,267 --> 00:28:25,567
to our business partners?

519
00:28:25,937 --> 00:28:27,107
Yes, that's it.

520
00:28:27,507 --> 00:28:30,277
That health supplement you sent under your name.

521
00:28:30,547 --> 00:28:31,647
Yes, I remember.

522
00:28:31,777 --> 00:28:32,777
Was it a coincidence?

523
00:28:33,177 --> 00:28:35,077
- What? - Are you telling me...

524
00:28:35,077 --> 00:28:37,317
that when you found out your son wasn't biologically yours,

525
00:28:37,787 --> 00:28:40,087
and happened to run into a pregnant Mi Young,

526
00:28:40,157 --> 00:28:41,757
you sent her that supplement...

527
00:28:42,117 --> 00:28:43,357
purely by coincidence?

528
00:28:44,257 --> 00:28:46,157
I'm sorry, what are you trying to say?

529
00:28:46,257 --> 00:28:48,257
She lost the baby because of that supplement.

530
00:28:48,797 --> 00:28:50,167
Lost the baby?

531
00:28:50,227 --> 00:28:52,067
At least, that's what Mi Young believes.

532
00:28:52,397 --> 00:28:54,497
That she miscarried after taking it.

533
00:28:54,567 --> 00:28:56,537
So she's been suspecting me as the one who gave it to her,

534
00:28:56,597 --> 00:28:58,267
and blaming me all this time.

535
00:28:58,337 --> 00:28:59,807
No, that can't be.

536
00:29:00,837 --> 00:29:03,437
That supplement was just a common something anyone can take...

537
00:29:03,507 --> 00:29:05,907
Sure, the supplement itself was probably harmless.

538
00:29:06,607 --> 00:29:08,847
Unless someone tampered with it.

539
00:29:10,417 --> 00:29:11,547
Tampered with it?

540
00:29:11,687 --> 00:29:12,817
Yes.

541
00:29:12,987 --> 00:29:16,157
- Tampered with it. - So you're saying, Ji Won Ho,

542
00:29:16,517 --> 00:29:18,787
that in order to harm Mi Young's baby,

543
00:29:18,857 --> 00:29:22,157
I deliberately tampered with the supplement.

544
00:29:22,897 --> 00:29:24,167
Is that what you're trying to say?

545
00:29:24,167 --> 00:29:25,167
Other than that possibility,

546
00:29:25,167 --> 00:29:27,537
I can't see any other way to explain this.

547
00:29:30,867 --> 00:29:31,937
If so,

548
00:29:32,437 --> 00:29:34,337
does that make you feel better?

549
00:29:35,037 --> 00:29:36,037
What?

550
00:29:36,107 --> 00:29:37,707
If Mi Young miscarried because she took...

551
00:29:37,777 --> 00:29:39,377
the supplement I happened to give her,

552
00:29:39,577 --> 00:29:40,877
and if the fact that she lost her child...

553
00:29:40,877 --> 00:29:42,817
and has a wound that will never heal...

554
00:29:42,917 --> 00:29:44,117
is all my fault,

555
00:29:44,347 --> 00:29:47,657
I'm asking if that would make you feel much better.

556
00:29:47,717 --> 00:29:48,717
Stop talking nonsense.

557
00:29:48,787 --> 00:29:51,787
- Just answer my question. - I think you should leave now.

558
00:29:52,427 --> 00:29:54,457
Any more conversation would be a waste of time.

559
00:29:56,757 --> 00:29:58,227
You tampered with it, didn't you?

560
00:30:02,367 --> 00:30:03,467
If Mi Young didn't have a child,

561
00:30:03,537 --> 00:30:05,407
it would be easier for you to get her back after the divorce,

562
00:30:05,467 --> 00:30:06,867
wouldn't it?

563
00:30:07,077 --> 00:30:09,477
You're the one who did it, you bastard.

564
00:30:09,537 --> 00:30:10,647
Am I wrong?

565
00:30:12,547 --> 00:30:13,547
Hey, you.

566
00:30:14,147 --> 00:30:15,277
Get your hands off me.

567
00:30:15,617 --> 00:30:16,817
Why do you think...

568
00:30:17,187 --> 00:30:20,187
I just stood by and watched Mi Young marry a scumbag like you?

569
00:30:20,787 --> 00:30:22,757
Because Mi Young chose you.

570
00:30:23,287 --> 00:30:25,957
Because you were the one Mi Young wanted.

571
00:30:26,757 --> 00:30:27,927
Listen to me.

572
00:30:28,697 --> 00:30:31,827
I would die for Mi Young.

573
00:30:32,127 --> 00:30:34,837
Unlike you, who'd shamelessly cheat on her.

574
00:30:34,967 --> 00:30:36,737
I'm nothing like you.

575
00:30:40,437 --> 00:30:41,577
Darn it.

576
00:30:51,517 --> 00:30:54,317
Ouch, that hurts. Gosh, that hurts.

577
00:30:55,387 --> 00:30:56,887
He could've just used his words.

578
00:30:56,957 --> 00:30:58,687
What is he, a gangster or something?

579
00:30:59,357 --> 00:31:00,997
And he's freakishly strong.

580
00:31:03,257 --> 00:31:04,567
Are you okay?

581
00:31:07,897 --> 00:31:10,307
What? You haven't left yet?

582
00:31:15,177 --> 00:31:17,677
But didn't you say Calvin fired you?

583
00:31:18,347 --> 00:31:19,347
I was.

584
00:31:19,677 --> 00:31:21,677
That's why you helped me out.

585
00:31:22,277 --> 00:31:23,887
What are you doing here anyway?

586
00:31:23,947 --> 00:31:25,117
Is there something you need?

587
00:31:25,417 --> 00:31:27,087
I'm here to investigate the case.

588
00:31:27,157 --> 00:31:30,487
Calvin is my prime murder suspect.

589
00:31:31,057 --> 00:31:32,057
What?

590
00:31:32,327 --> 00:31:34,557
When I was pushed off the cliff the other day,

591
00:31:34,957 --> 00:31:36,257
Calvin was...

592
00:31:36,797 --> 00:31:38,297
behind it.

593
00:31:39,367 --> 00:31:40,897
No way.

594
00:31:40,967 --> 00:31:44,407
It's true. You just saw for yourself, CEO Ji.

595
00:31:44,737 --> 00:31:47,337
He grabs you by the collar just for saying a few words.

596
00:31:47,837 --> 00:31:49,907
Getting rid of someone...

597
00:31:50,077 --> 00:31:51,507
would be nothing to a guy like him.

598
00:31:51,677 --> 00:31:52,707
That's true.

599
00:31:52,947 --> 00:31:54,947
That guy has serious anger management issues.

600
00:31:55,017 --> 00:31:57,347
I'm serious, I almost suffocated just now.

601
00:31:57,587 --> 00:32:00,787
That prank must have been Calvin's doing too.

602
00:32:01,087 --> 00:32:02,087
Wait a minute...

603
00:32:02,217 --> 00:32:04,527
Were you outside listening to all of that?

604
00:32:04,627 --> 00:32:06,357
I wasn't trying to listen,

605
00:32:06,827 --> 00:32:08,897
but I couldn't help hearing it.

606
00:32:10,627 --> 00:32:13,127
But seeing him get so fired up like that...

607
00:32:13,367 --> 00:32:14,937
makes me think it might not be him.

608
00:32:15,197 --> 00:32:16,967
This is so confusing.

609
00:32:17,037 --> 00:32:18,337
There's nothing to be confused about.

610
00:32:18,967 --> 00:32:20,237
Without a doubt,

611
00:32:20,307 --> 00:32:21,737
Calvin is the culprit.

612
00:32:23,877 --> 00:32:27,147
When you're this stressed out, you have to eat to feel better.

613
00:32:27,777 --> 00:32:29,217
Let's go get something good to eat.

614
00:32:30,387 --> 00:32:31,487
I can't.

615
00:32:31,947 --> 00:32:32,947
Why not?

616
00:32:33,017 --> 00:32:35,787
I said I can't. Not until I clear my name.

617
00:32:36,017 --> 00:32:39,587
- Clear your name? - My wife thinks I'm a murderer.

618
00:32:39,757 --> 00:32:41,327
Until I catch the real culprit behind the miscarriage...

619
00:32:41,397 --> 00:32:43,297
and clear my name,

620
00:32:43,697 --> 00:32:46,397
- let's not see each other. - Why?

621
00:32:46,667 --> 00:32:48,367
What does you being falsely accused...

622
00:32:48,437 --> 00:32:50,567
have to do with us seeing each other?

623
00:32:50,637 --> 00:32:53,567
It has everything to do with it. This is all your fault.

624
00:32:53,937 --> 00:32:55,807
My wife blew up because of you,

625
00:32:55,877 --> 00:32:57,407
and that's how this mess started.

626
00:32:57,407 --> 00:32:58,747
What do you mean?

627
00:32:58,847 --> 00:33:00,777
Anyway, I'm leaving.

628
00:33:02,547 --> 00:33:04,547
Hey, wait up.

629
00:33:11,757 --> 00:33:13,157
Hey. CEO Ji.

630
00:33:14,427 --> 00:33:17,027
Hey, seriously.

631
00:33:28,577 --> 00:33:31,447
Please give it some more thought.

632
00:33:31,477 --> 00:33:33,407
It will look even more spectacular under the lights.

633
00:33:33,577 --> 00:33:35,347
So please take that into consideration.

634
00:33:35,477 --> 00:33:37,217
Think it over...

635
00:33:39,747 --> 00:33:42,017
You have hands, and you have feet...

636
00:33:42,457 --> 00:33:45,527
My dear Dallae, when did you grow so much?

637
00:33:46,787 --> 00:33:48,457
Just hang in there a little longer.

638
00:33:48,857 --> 00:33:52,327
When you're born, Mommy will take even better care of you.

639
00:33:55,837 --> 00:33:58,207
- CEO Baek. - Oh, yes. Come in.

640
00:33:58,337 --> 00:34:00,367
(CEO's Office)

641
00:34:00,977 --> 00:34:03,207
I hope I'm not interrupting.

642
00:34:03,877 --> 00:34:04,907
Not at all.

643
00:34:05,507 --> 00:34:07,047
What can I do for you?

644
00:34:07,577 --> 00:34:09,017
Oh, well...

645
00:34:14,587 --> 00:34:16,917
What is this?

646
00:34:25,327 --> 00:34:26,397
Goodbye.

647
00:34:28,737 --> 00:34:29,737
CEO Baek.

648
00:34:30,937 --> 00:34:32,267
It was a massive success.

649
00:34:32,507 --> 00:34:34,037
All the clients who had fittings today...

650
00:34:34,107 --> 00:34:35,877
loved their dresses so much...

651
00:34:35,937 --> 00:34:37,207
that they booked with us on the spot.

652
00:34:37,877 --> 00:34:41,677
Even a client who'd been shopping around for a while...

653
00:34:41,747 --> 00:34:43,717
booked with us the minute she walked in today.

654
00:34:43,947 --> 00:34:46,017
Really? That's wonderful.

655
00:34:46,247 --> 00:34:49,357
It really reminds me how incredible CEO Ji is.

656
00:34:49,517 --> 00:34:52,557
I mean, it doesn't seem like he does much,

657
00:34:52,957 --> 00:34:56,057
but he still manages to create these perfect dresses every season.

658
00:34:56,627 --> 00:34:57,767
Don't you agree, CEO Baek?

659
00:34:58,667 --> 00:34:59,667
Yes.

660
00:35:01,197 --> 00:35:04,267
By the way, Vice President Kang...

661
00:35:05,407 --> 00:35:09,137
There's something I'd like to ask you...

662
00:35:10,177 --> 00:35:11,177
What is it?

663
00:35:12,677 --> 00:35:13,707
Well...

664
00:35:16,247 --> 00:35:17,417
Just a moment.

665
00:35:19,847 --> 00:35:20,957
Hello?

666
00:35:23,257 --> 00:35:24,287
Welcome.

667
00:35:37,537 --> 00:35:39,267
Ji Won Ho...

668
00:35:39,837 --> 00:35:41,437
came to see me today.

669
00:35:41,837 --> 00:35:42,937
Won Ho did?

670
00:35:44,147 --> 00:35:46,377
Why? What was it about?

671
00:35:46,807 --> 00:35:48,277
He asked about the supplements...

672
00:35:48,747 --> 00:35:51,417
I sent to your company about three years ago.

673
00:35:52,087 --> 00:35:53,087
Supplements?

674
00:35:53,147 --> 00:35:54,517
The one I sent three years ago during the holidays,

675
00:35:54,517 --> 00:35:56,717
under the Calvin Hotel name.

676
00:35:57,117 --> 00:35:58,127
Don't you remember?

677
00:35:58,957 --> 00:36:01,297
It was a health supplement in a purple container.

678
00:36:01,727 --> 00:36:03,027
Could it be...

679
00:36:03,327 --> 00:36:06,297
similar to that supplement you gave me before?

680
00:36:06,567 --> 00:36:07,637
Yes, that's the one.

681
00:36:09,367 --> 00:36:10,667
Take this when you feel tired.

682
00:36:11,467 --> 00:36:12,467
Thanks.

683
00:36:19,707 --> 00:36:21,077
(Energy Care Up)

684
00:36:23,117 --> 00:36:24,187
Because of those pills...

685
00:36:25,047 --> 00:36:26,087
That's impossible.

686
00:36:28,757 --> 00:36:30,957
I never even opened the box.

687
00:36:32,657 --> 00:36:33,657
So of course,

688
00:36:35,227 --> 00:36:36,257
I never took it.

689
00:36:40,327 --> 00:36:42,597
- Really? - That supplement...

690
00:36:43,567 --> 00:36:46,007
was made by a company affiliated with Calvin.

691
00:36:47,237 --> 00:36:50,307
Back then, I felt too resentful toward you.

692
00:36:52,647 --> 00:36:53,647
I'm sorry.

693
00:37:01,517 --> 00:37:02,557
What's wrong?

694
00:37:03,617 --> 00:37:04,627
I'm sorry, Mi Young.

695
00:37:06,357 --> 00:37:07,527
I'm so sorry.

696
00:37:09,257 --> 00:37:11,067
When I found out you were pregnant,

697
00:37:12,167 --> 00:37:14,097
I didn't want you to have a healthy baby.

698
00:37:16,397 --> 00:37:17,467
That child...

699
00:37:18,867 --> 00:37:20,367
could have been my child.

700
00:37:23,107 --> 00:37:24,377
To be honest, I was angry.

701
00:37:26,707 --> 00:37:27,847
I guess I wanted you...

702
00:37:29,617 --> 00:37:30,817
to suffer just like I was.

703
00:37:34,887 --> 00:37:37,627
Because I had such awful thoughts about you then,

704
00:37:39,657 --> 00:37:41,357
I feel like I'm the reason that happened to your child.

705
00:37:43,527 --> 00:37:44,567
Don't say that.

706
00:37:46,597 --> 00:37:47,937
It's not your fault.

707
00:37:58,147 --> 00:37:59,777
How could you even think that?

708
00:38:00,507 --> 00:38:02,347
What? What is it now?

709
00:38:02,547 --> 00:38:04,147
I heard you went to see Calvin.

710
00:38:05,147 --> 00:38:06,917
Is Calvin some kind of criminal?

711
00:38:07,787 --> 00:38:09,957
How can you even imagine something so ridiculous?

712
00:38:10,257 --> 00:38:11,927
Gosh. You called me a murderer,

713
00:38:11,987 --> 00:38:13,657
but Calvin isn't even a criminal to you?

714
00:38:14,357 --> 00:38:16,557
I didn't realise Calvin was such a wonderful person.

715
00:38:17,927 --> 00:38:21,097
In any case, you're barking up the wrong tree.

716
00:38:21,897 --> 00:38:24,767
The medication I took has nothing to do with Calvin.

717
00:38:25,907 --> 00:38:28,907
Then what is it? Stop beating around the bush...

718
00:38:28,977 --> 00:38:30,537
and just spit it out.

719
00:38:30,947 --> 00:38:33,407
What pill did you take, and how?

720
00:38:33,577 --> 00:38:34,577
That...

721
00:38:37,117 --> 00:38:38,717
Ask your friend yourself.

722
00:38:39,017 --> 00:38:40,017
What? My friend?

723
00:38:41,187 --> 00:38:43,857
I really have no idea what you're talking about.

724
00:38:48,597 --> 00:38:50,157
Okay. Let me ask you one more thing.

725
00:38:51,427 --> 00:38:53,597
Do you really still think I'm a murderer?

726
00:38:53,727 --> 00:38:54,737
The one who killed our baby?

727
00:38:59,607 --> 00:39:00,607
Then there's nothing I can do.

728
00:39:01,007 --> 00:39:02,007
I'll have to move out again.

729
00:39:03,337 --> 00:39:04,477
You're moving out again?

730
00:39:05,947 --> 00:39:07,307
Well, can you keep living in the same house...

731
00:39:07,377 --> 00:39:08,377
with a murderer like me?

732
00:39:08,717 --> 00:39:10,987
You're thrilled that I called you a murderer, aren't you?

733
00:39:11,747 --> 00:39:12,747
What?

734
00:39:12,917 --> 00:39:13,917
It's true, isn't it?

735
00:39:14,117 --> 00:39:15,287
You're using that as an excuse to move out...

736
00:39:15,917 --> 00:39:18,057
so you can live with that girl, Hee Ju.

737
00:39:18,387 --> 00:39:19,957
You pretend to be mad at me,

738
00:39:20,327 --> 00:39:21,857
but that was your real goal, wasn't it?

739
00:39:21,997 --> 00:39:22,997
Whatever.

740
00:39:23,427 --> 00:39:24,997
You'd better think about how you're going...

741
00:39:25,067 --> 00:39:26,097
to handle the consequences.

742
00:39:26,997 --> 00:39:28,267
Why would I have to deal with them?

743
00:39:28,367 --> 00:39:31,007
No, you're absolutely going to have to.

744
00:39:31,207 --> 00:39:32,837
Because I'm going to shatter this...

745
00:39:33,007 --> 00:39:34,677
ridiculous delusion of yours completely.

746
00:39:51,857 --> 00:39:53,487
What am I supposed to do now?

747
00:39:54,557 --> 00:39:56,627
I talked a big game before I left,

748
00:39:56,827 --> 00:39:59,027
but I really don't know what Mi Young is thinking.

749
00:39:59,797 --> 00:40:01,067
So, your wife...

750
00:40:01,837 --> 00:40:04,407
never told you what kind of pills they were, right?

751
00:40:05,167 --> 00:40:06,567
Right.

752
00:40:06,907 --> 00:40:10,037
She just told me to ask my friend without any details.

753
00:40:10,337 --> 00:40:12,977
She just keeps talking in riddles.

754
00:40:13,447 --> 00:40:15,777
Honestly, who else is in my life? It's just you, Kyung Tae.

755
00:40:16,747 --> 00:40:19,817
That's true. I'm your only friend.

756
00:40:20,317 --> 00:40:22,957
Anyway, it's a huge relief it wasn't from A Ri,

757
00:40:24,227 --> 00:40:26,287
but now I really don't know what to do.

758
00:40:27,087 --> 00:40:29,127
I looked into it a bit after we talked,

759
00:40:29,857 --> 00:40:33,267
and there are tons of foods to avoid during pregnancy.

760
00:40:35,267 --> 00:40:36,297
Maybe your wife...

761
00:40:37,767 --> 00:40:39,567
just wants to put the blame on you.

762
00:40:40,307 --> 00:40:41,737
If she accepts that the miscarriage is her fault,

763
00:40:42,977 --> 00:40:44,207
it would be too hard for her to bear.

764
00:40:46,147 --> 00:40:47,247
You have a point.

765
00:40:47,847 --> 00:40:50,517
Maybe you should just let this go for now...

766
00:40:51,717 --> 00:40:53,547
and finalise the lawsuit on good terms.

767
00:40:54,417 --> 00:40:55,687
Wouldn't that be better for both of you?

768
00:40:57,217 --> 00:40:58,457
You're both in the same industry,

769
00:40:59,027 --> 00:41:00,897
so you'll still be entangled even after the divorce.

770
00:41:00,957 --> 00:41:02,557
I don't want to take it this far either.

771
00:41:02,627 --> 00:41:04,827
But Baek Mi Young keeps testing me.

772
00:41:05,067 --> 00:41:06,927
Hey, she called me a murderer.

773
00:41:06,997 --> 00:41:08,697
How am I supposed to just sit back and take that?

774
00:41:08,897 --> 00:41:11,437
She probably just said that out of anger over Hee Ju.

775
00:41:12,067 --> 00:41:14,107
If you just cut ties with Hee Ju...

776
00:41:14,167 --> 00:41:15,277
This isn't about Hee Ju.

777
00:41:15,337 --> 00:41:17,237
I'm going to get to the bottom of this no matter what.

778
00:41:17,307 --> 00:41:18,707
I'll get to the bottom of it,

779
00:41:18,877 --> 00:41:21,617
and I'll prove my innocence to Baek Mi Young once and for all.

780
00:42:06,887 --> 00:42:08,197
Back when I had my miscarriage,

781
00:42:09,027 --> 00:42:11,567
I confirmed it with my doctor at the time.

782
00:42:13,267 --> 00:42:15,037
I found out that the medication my husband gave me then...

783
00:42:16,297 --> 00:42:18,137
was fatal to the fetus...

784
00:42:18,207 --> 00:42:21,007
What is this bullshit? What do you think you're doing?

785
00:42:34,317 --> 00:42:35,387
Why do you think...

786
00:42:35,917 --> 00:42:38,687
I just stood by and watched Mi Young marry a scumbag like you?

787
00:42:40,057 --> 00:42:41,797
Because Mi Young chose you.

788
00:42:42,597 --> 00:42:45,027
Because you were the one Mi Young wanted.

789
00:43:19,867 --> 00:43:20,927
Do you really not remember?

790
00:43:21,667 --> 00:43:23,167
Pills or whatever else,

791
00:43:23,237 --> 00:43:25,907
I never gave you anything that could have harmed you.

792
00:43:32,747 --> 00:43:33,747
Then there's nothing I can do.

793
00:43:34,207 --> 00:43:35,217
I'll have to move out again.

794
00:43:36,417 --> 00:43:37,577
You're moving out again?

795
00:43:38,647 --> 00:43:40,017
Well, can you keep living in the same house...

796
00:43:40,017 --> 00:43:41,287
with a murderer like me?

797
00:44:05,547 --> 00:44:08,217
(Off Air)

798
00:44:36,607 --> 00:44:37,607
It's cold.

799
00:44:39,607 --> 00:44:41,677
I'm freezing. Why isn't he here yet?

800
00:44:43,377 --> 00:44:44,377
Hey.

801
00:44:44,917 --> 00:44:46,047
Oh, come on.

802
00:44:46,817 --> 00:44:48,557
Hey. Sorry I'm a little late.

803
00:44:48,687 --> 00:44:50,757
You asked me to meet you, and you're the one who's late?

804
00:44:51,017 --> 00:44:54,427
Sorry. I promise we'll have a good time today.

805
00:44:54,627 --> 00:44:55,897
This had better be fun.

806
00:44:56,127 --> 00:44:58,097
- Let's go. - Where are we going?

807
00:44:58,167 --> 00:44:59,527
- To play a game. - What game?

808
00:44:59,867 --> 00:45:02,137
(Bowling)

809
00:45:12,007 --> 00:45:13,807
What's wrong? Are you tired?

810
00:45:14,407 --> 00:45:15,517
Yes, a little.

811
00:45:15,617 --> 00:45:16,977
This is when I'm usually fast asleep.

812
00:45:17,247 --> 00:45:18,787
That's your problem.

813
00:45:19,417 --> 00:45:21,187
When you work, you work like crazy,

814
00:45:21,417 --> 00:45:23,187
and when you rest, you sleep like a log.

815
00:45:23,487 --> 00:45:25,327
When do you ever have any fun?

816
00:45:25,387 --> 00:45:27,087
That's why I came out tonight.

817
00:45:27,687 --> 00:45:31,367
Exactly. Let's unwind for a change,

818
00:45:31,427 --> 00:45:33,227
and blow off some steam.

819
00:45:33,767 --> 00:45:35,667
- Okay? - Deal.

820
00:45:39,137 --> 00:45:41,107
They should be here any minute.

821
00:45:42,237 --> 00:45:43,237
Is someone else coming?

822
00:45:45,677 --> 00:45:47,747
Oh, wait. They're here.

823
00:45:48,517 --> 00:45:49,777
Vice President Kang, over here.

824
00:45:52,447 --> 00:45:53,447
You...

825
00:45:53,517 --> 00:45:56,357
- A Ri, I can't believe you. - Just hold on.

826
00:45:59,627 --> 00:46:01,397
- I'm leaving. - Hey, what's wrong?

827
00:46:01,457 --> 00:46:02,797
Don't be like that. Let's just have fun.

828
00:46:02,857 --> 00:46:04,427
Why would you do something I didn't ask for?

829
00:46:04,497 --> 00:46:05,967
Just one game. Please?

830
00:46:06,397 --> 00:46:07,497
Seriously.

831
00:46:09,037 --> 00:46:10,067
Come on.

832
00:46:13,967 --> 00:46:15,777
Sorry we're a little late.

833
00:46:15,977 --> 00:46:18,647
No, you're right on time.

834
00:46:19,547 --> 00:46:22,647
Great, we can make teams and get started.

835
00:46:22,717 --> 00:46:24,417
A Ri, what do you think you're doing?

836
00:46:24,947 --> 00:46:26,347
Are you really going to do this?

837
00:46:26,517 --> 00:46:27,517
I'm sorry.

838
00:46:27,787 --> 00:46:30,357
I knew you both wouldn't have come if I told you beforehand.

839
00:46:30,457 --> 00:46:32,227
- Then why did you? - You knew better, so why do this?

840
00:46:32,527 --> 00:46:34,527
Can't you two just make up?

841
00:46:35,227 --> 00:46:37,157
It's not just me. The entire J&White family...

842
00:46:37,557 --> 00:46:39,167
is walking on eggshells around you two.

843
00:46:39,527 --> 00:46:40,927
He's right.

844
00:46:41,337 --> 00:46:43,637
Let's just call today a company workshop.

845
00:46:43,697 --> 00:46:45,307
Think of it that way.

846
00:46:45,667 --> 00:46:47,807
We can play some games and build our teamwork.

847
00:46:48,307 --> 00:46:49,837
What do you say, CEO Ji?

848
00:46:51,347 --> 00:46:53,677
Well, I don't really mind, but...

849
00:46:54,847 --> 00:46:57,647
All right. Then, just like Director Song said,

850
00:46:58,547 --> 00:47:00,987
we'll think of it as a workshop.

851
00:47:02,217 --> 00:47:04,787
Great. Then shall we get started?

852
00:47:05,057 --> 00:47:06,857
The losing team buys drinks.

853
00:47:07,227 --> 00:47:08,227
Okay.

854
00:47:18,367 --> 00:47:20,167
- Okay. - Nice one.

855
00:47:32,487 --> 00:47:33,547
What was that?

856
00:47:57,877 --> 00:47:59,207
Yes!

857
00:48:00,677 --> 00:48:02,517
(Won Ho, Mi Young, Kyung Tae, A Ri)

858
00:48:18,867 --> 00:48:20,327
I told you to follow through.

859
00:48:20,497 --> 00:48:22,737
Why are you doing it like that? Do it like this.

860
00:48:25,407 --> 00:48:26,407
Fine.

861
00:48:29,107 --> 00:48:30,107
Let's go.

862
00:48:43,057 --> 00:48:44,057
Us too.

863
00:48:46,187 --> 00:48:47,187
Nice.

864
00:48:47,587 --> 00:48:49,827
Yes!

865
00:48:49,897 --> 00:48:51,127
Look at that.

866
00:48:52,697 --> 00:48:54,497
This is the last one.

867
00:48:55,867 --> 00:48:58,507
As long as Mi Young doesn't get a strike,

868
00:48:58,567 --> 00:49:00,167
we win.

869
00:49:00,237 --> 00:49:01,307
Okay, let's do this.

870
00:49:01,507 --> 00:49:03,707
- It won't be easy. - We won this.

871
00:49:03,777 --> 00:49:04,777
Baek Mi Young.

872
00:49:05,307 --> 00:49:06,307
Let's go.

873
00:49:17,087 --> 00:49:19,327
Come on...

874
00:49:20,427 --> 00:49:21,427
Okay!

875
00:49:26,967 --> 00:49:27,967
Yes!

876
00:49:29,367 --> 00:49:30,697
- Boom. Yes. - Bang!

877
00:49:32,107 --> 00:49:34,537
- Cheers, everyone. - Cheers.

878
00:49:41,817 --> 00:49:43,077
Goodness.

879
00:49:44,117 --> 00:49:46,147
Another beer over here.

880
00:49:46,517 --> 00:49:48,957
Gosh, Director Song. You're really going for it tonight.

881
00:49:49,517 --> 00:49:51,217
Are you okay?

882
00:49:51,457 --> 00:49:53,557
Of course.

883
00:49:53,627 --> 00:49:55,597
I'm Song A Ri.

884
00:49:55,757 --> 00:49:59,427
A little beer is nothing.

885
00:49:59,667 --> 00:50:01,397
We can tell you're really drunk.

886
00:50:01,797 --> 00:50:02,797
You should stop drinking now.

887
00:50:02,867 --> 00:50:06,037
You can tell I'm not drunk at all.

888
00:50:08,777 --> 00:50:10,137
Where are we?

889
00:50:11,137 --> 00:50:12,647
What round is this?

890
00:50:12,707 --> 00:50:13,707
What?

891
00:50:14,247 --> 00:50:16,477
Director Song, let's call it a night.

892
00:50:17,077 --> 00:50:19,087
I'll get Director Song a taxi and be right back.

893
00:50:19,417 --> 00:50:20,587
Can you manage on your own?

894
00:50:21,047 --> 00:50:23,057
- Should I go with you? - No, it's fine.

895
00:50:23,457 --> 00:50:25,527
You two can talk while I'm gone.

896
00:50:25,727 --> 00:50:26,757
Let's go, Director Song.

897
00:50:26,757 --> 00:50:28,197
- Let's go. - Are we going to round three?

898
00:50:28,257 --> 00:50:29,257
- Come on, let's go. - Goodness.

899
00:50:29,327 --> 00:50:30,897
- Nice! - Come on, we have to go.

900
00:50:30,957 --> 00:50:32,727
- Let's go for round four. - Careful.

901
00:50:32,797 --> 00:50:33,867
We have to make it to round four.

902
00:50:45,907 --> 00:50:46,947
Come back home.

903
00:50:49,017 --> 00:50:51,987
- Are you serious? - You can't keep living in a motel.

904
00:50:52,417 --> 00:50:54,447
It's not like I intentionally kicked you out.

905
00:50:55,017 --> 00:50:57,087
Then what about when you called me a murderer?

906
00:50:57,717 --> 00:50:58,827
Are you taking that back too?

907
00:50:59,557 --> 00:51:00,557
What?

908
00:51:00,687 --> 00:51:02,927
There has to be a reason you're suddenly acting like this.

909
00:51:03,257 --> 00:51:05,267
Have you cleared up your misunderstandings about me?

910
00:51:05,497 --> 00:51:08,027
Does this mean I don't have to hear about those pills anymore?

911
00:51:08,697 --> 00:51:09,697
About the pills?

912
00:51:13,467 --> 00:51:15,177
If you don't want to come home, then don't.

913
00:51:15,337 --> 00:51:17,677
Just keep living at the motel and fooling around with Hee Ju.

914
00:51:17,807 --> 00:51:19,247
Are you messing with me right now?

915
00:51:19,307 --> 00:51:20,807
Why do you keep going back and forth?

916
00:51:20,877 --> 00:51:23,447
And why can't you get it through your thick skull?

917
00:51:23,517 --> 00:51:26,247
What did you just say? Hey, are you done?

918
00:51:26,317 --> 00:51:28,047
I'm done. You look like you're about to hit me.

919
00:51:28,117 --> 00:51:29,257
Go on, hit me.

920
00:51:29,457 --> 00:51:31,757
Here. Is this what you want? Happy now?

921
00:51:31,827 --> 00:51:35,097
- Fine. Do whatever you want. - It hurts. My head hurts.

922
00:51:37,697 --> 00:51:39,527
Why are you two acting like this?

923
00:51:42,637 --> 00:51:44,497
You promised to part with a smile.

924
00:51:46,437 --> 00:51:47,437
This won't do.

925
00:51:47,907 --> 00:51:49,407
I'll just have to force you to smile.

926
00:51:50,277 --> 00:51:51,277
Excuse me, ma'am.

927
00:51:52,747 --> 00:51:55,047
Sorry to bother you, but could you take a picture for us?

928
00:51:55,117 --> 00:51:56,477
Why are we suddenly taking a picture?

929
00:51:56,477 --> 00:51:58,487
Won Ho, get in closer. Mi Young, closer.

930
00:51:58,547 --> 00:52:00,217
Okay, everyone, look over there and smile.

931
00:52:00,447 --> 00:52:03,087
Okay, I'm taking the picture. One, two, three.

932
00:52:11,427 --> 00:52:13,227
You and Mi Young should share a taxi.

933
00:52:14,467 --> 00:52:15,467
What are you talking about?

934
00:52:15,867 --> 00:52:18,237
Hurry and go make things right with Mi Young.

935
00:52:22,737 --> 00:52:25,177
- Go on. Hurry up. - Unbelievable.

936
00:52:33,247 --> 00:52:34,247
Hey.

937
00:52:34,987 --> 00:52:38,017
- Oh my gosh, are you okay? - Darn it.

938
00:52:38,327 --> 00:52:39,427
- Are you okay? - Darn it.

939
00:52:39,487 --> 00:52:40,487
What happened?

940
00:52:40,557 --> 00:52:42,657
My coat got caught in the door, and I was trying to pull it out...

941
00:52:43,127 --> 00:52:44,197
Are you okay? What do I do?

942
00:52:44,257 --> 00:52:46,697
- Go, just go. - You should go, Mi Young.

943
00:52:46,767 --> 00:52:48,067
I'll take him home.

944
00:52:48,437 --> 00:52:49,737
I'm so sorry.

945
00:52:56,007 --> 00:52:57,807
Hey, let me see. Does it hurt a lot?

946
00:52:58,207 --> 00:52:59,577
Of course it hurts!

947
00:53:00,807 --> 00:53:01,817
Does it hurt that much?

948
00:53:02,277 --> 00:53:03,717
(Calvin)

949
00:53:08,517 --> 00:53:10,917
- Hello? - You must still be sleeping.

950
00:53:12,187 --> 00:53:14,127
What? Why are you calling?

951
00:53:15,197 --> 00:53:16,427
You didn't find the evidence, did you?

952
00:53:17,057 --> 00:53:18,327
I'm about to find it.

953
00:53:18,467 --> 00:53:19,967
I have the evidence.

954
00:53:20,697 --> 00:53:24,037
- What? - You have neither ability nor will.

955
00:53:24,697 --> 00:53:27,337
I figured you'd just go around stirring up trouble.

956
00:53:27,837 --> 00:53:29,537
So I just found the evidence myself.

957
00:53:31,507 --> 00:53:33,807
I'll give you two hours. Come and get it.

958
00:53:39,747 --> 00:53:40,947
It's just the angle...

959
00:53:41,317 --> 00:53:42,517
Why? Is there a problem?

960
00:53:42,687 --> 00:53:44,187
It looks like they're kissing, but...

961
00:53:44,687 --> 00:53:46,157
it wasn't captured very well on camera.

962
00:53:46,557 --> 00:53:47,757
I see that.

963
00:53:48,657 --> 00:53:51,157
If that couple comes again, I'll let you know.

964
00:53:51,727 --> 00:53:52,727
Thank you.

965
00:53:57,637 --> 00:53:58,637
But...

966
00:53:59,067 --> 00:54:01,307
I feel bad that I keep getting your help.

967
00:54:01,677 --> 00:54:04,107
Not at all. I do it because I want to.

968
00:54:05,607 --> 00:54:07,847
You want to?

969
00:54:14,887 --> 00:54:16,187
You cut your hair.

970
00:54:16,357 --> 00:54:17,957
It looks really good on you.

971
00:54:18,017 --> 00:54:19,227
It's pretty. Very pretty.

972
00:54:19,557 --> 00:54:21,587
- It's pretty? - Yes.

973
00:54:29,597 --> 00:54:31,037
Oh, right. There's something...

974
00:54:31,097 --> 00:54:33,167
I'd like to ask for your legal advice on.

975
00:54:33,637 --> 00:54:34,637
Yes.

976
00:54:35,377 --> 00:54:37,577
If you have any questions, feel free to ask me anything.

977
00:54:37,707 --> 00:54:42,917
Yes. How would I remove a guest from their room?

978
00:54:42,977 --> 00:54:44,547
Are you talking about a forced eviction?

979
00:54:44,717 --> 00:54:47,017
Yes, a forced eviction. How do I make that happen?

980
00:54:47,817 --> 00:54:49,587
If they're a wanted fugitive on the run...

981
00:54:49,657 --> 00:54:51,287
or if they've caused property damage,

982
00:54:51,357 --> 00:54:52,927
like vandalizing things in the room, you can.

983
00:54:53,957 --> 00:54:56,697
What if the guest is just a bad person?

984
00:54:56,757 --> 00:54:59,097
Would that be considered grounds for a forced eviction?

985
00:54:59,397 --> 00:55:00,567
A bad person?

986
00:55:01,627 --> 00:55:02,967
That's a bit of a gray area.

987
00:55:03,637 --> 00:55:04,637
Why?

988
00:55:04,797 --> 00:55:07,107
Is there a problem guest in this building?

989
00:55:07,367 --> 00:55:09,977
We offered a full refund, but they're refusing to leave,

990
00:55:10,137 --> 00:55:11,577
and they're threatening my mother and me.

991
00:55:11,777 --> 00:55:12,777
Threatening you?

992
00:55:13,677 --> 00:55:14,677
That person over there.

993
00:55:15,747 --> 00:55:17,777
- Excuse me, miss. - Ahn Hee Ju.

994
00:55:18,747 --> 00:55:19,747
Yes?

995
00:55:30,657 --> 00:55:31,657
A lawyer?

996
00:55:32,267 --> 00:55:33,927
Right now, my client is...

997
00:55:37,437 --> 00:55:38,937
It's Ahn Hee Ju.

998
00:55:40,637 --> 00:55:43,277
On the verge of pressing charges against you, Ahn Hee Ju.

999
00:55:43,637 --> 00:55:44,637
Press charges?

1000
00:55:49,417 --> 00:55:50,417
What is this?

1001
00:55:50,877 --> 00:55:53,017
I heard you threatened the owner.

1002
00:55:53,717 --> 00:55:57,017
- What? - Why do you insist on staying?

1003
00:55:58,757 --> 00:56:00,487
What is your reason for insisting on this specific motel?

1004
00:56:01,357 --> 00:56:04,327
Look. I'm a little busy right now.

1005
00:56:05,367 --> 00:56:08,097
I'll talk to you next time we meet.

1006
00:56:08,497 --> 00:56:10,097
You don't look that busy to me.

1007
00:56:10,337 --> 00:56:12,467
I'm on my way to catch a murderer.

1008
00:56:13,967 --> 00:56:14,967
A murderer?

1009
00:56:15,037 --> 00:56:16,437
If I let them get away,

1010
00:56:17,137 --> 00:56:18,647
are you going to catch them for me?

1011
00:56:22,117 --> 00:56:23,117
Gosh.

1012
00:56:26,887 --> 00:56:27,887
See what I mean?

1013
00:56:28,147 --> 00:56:30,987
She's a rotten person.

1014
00:56:31,927 --> 00:56:32,927
A what?

1015
00:56:33,487 --> 00:56:35,457
Oh, I said, rotten.

1016
00:56:36,797 --> 00:56:40,097
You're right. She is a completely rotten person.

1017
00:56:40,097 --> 00:56:41,167
Yes.

1018
00:56:46,067 --> 00:56:49,877
Take it. Icing it might help it heal faster.

1019
00:56:51,677 --> 00:56:54,447
It's a good thing you weren't cut.

1020
00:56:55,047 --> 00:56:56,877
Are you worried about me?

1021
00:56:57,917 --> 00:56:58,917
I'm going to go.

1022
00:56:59,347 --> 00:57:01,047
Can't you just tell me straight?

1023
00:57:10,097 --> 00:57:12,267
I'm talking about the pills you said you took three years ago.

1024
00:57:13,467 --> 00:57:16,067
Can't you stop being evasive and just tell me what happened?

1025
00:57:17,467 --> 00:57:19,607
I need to hear what on earth those pills you took were,

1026
00:57:19,667 --> 00:57:21,707
and why you keep calling me a murderer.

1027
00:57:21,767 --> 00:57:24,337
I need you to tell me first before I decide what to do.

1028
00:57:25,307 --> 00:57:26,307
Decide?

1029
00:57:26,547 --> 00:57:28,747
Whether I should keep denying it,

1030
00:57:31,447 --> 00:57:32,517
or if I should truly apologize...

1031
00:57:32,517 --> 00:57:34,617
and beg for your forgiveness on my knees.

1032
00:57:34,787 --> 00:57:36,157
You would beg for forgiveness?

1033
00:57:36,287 --> 00:57:37,317
If it really was my fault,

1034
00:57:37,417 --> 00:57:40,027
I'll admit it, no questions asked, and beg for your forgiveness.

1035
00:57:43,627 --> 00:57:44,627
So just tell me.

1036
00:57:45,797 --> 00:57:46,927
On that day three years ago,

1037
00:57:47,967 --> 00:57:49,497
what exactly were those pills you took?

1038
00:57:55,037 --> 00:57:56,177
No, wait...

1039
00:57:57,107 --> 00:57:58,107
Why is this person...

1040
00:57:58,607 --> 00:57:59,607
Are you disappointed...

1041
00:58:00,207 --> 00:58:03,317
that I wasn't the one who pushed you off the cliff?

1042
00:58:04,017 --> 00:58:05,017
Is this...

1043
00:58:06,217 --> 00:58:07,217
real?

1044
00:58:07,847 --> 00:58:09,017
You didn't fake this, did you?

1045
00:58:09,357 --> 00:58:10,987
If you're curious, go check for yourself.

1046
00:58:11,957 --> 00:58:13,987
Around the time you fell from the cliff,

1047
00:58:14,057 --> 00:58:15,597
within 30 minutes before and after,

1048
00:58:15,957 --> 00:58:17,827
only one person came down...

1049
00:58:18,527 --> 00:58:20,667
to the parking lot, besides the couple...

1050
00:58:20,727 --> 00:58:21,727
doing their wedding shoot.

1051
00:58:23,537 --> 00:58:24,537
That person.

1052
00:58:28,407 --> 00:58:30,137
This is as far as I can help you.

1053
00:58:31,377 --> 00:58:33,277
Whether you want revenge or retribution,

1054
00:58:33,807 --> 00:58:35,007
the rest is up to you.

1055
00:58:35,517 --> 00:58:36,747
It's none of my business.

1056
00:58:39,547 --> 00:58:42,257
I just don't understand why I should have to explain...

1057
00:58:42,487 --> 00:58:44,287
this to you.

1058
00:58:45,327 --> 00:58:46,657
Okay, I'm sorry too.

1059
00:58:47,227 --> 00:58:49,057
I'm sorry for the fact...

1060
00:58:49,697 --> 00:58:52,697
that you resent me this much, and I still have no idea why.

1061
00:58:53,597 --> 00:58:54,767
So, Mi Young.

1062
00:58:55,597 --> 00:58:57,367
Please, just tell me now.

1063
00:58:57,997 --> 00:59:00,537
What were the pills that gave you such a hard time?

1064
00:59:01,067 --> 00:59:03,577
I need to hear it directly from you, okay?

1065
00:59:12,247 --> 00:59:14,147
What put Dallae in danger was...

1066
00:59:15,317 --> 00:59:16,557
the herbal medicine.

1067
00:59:17,357 --> 00:59:18,827
Not the pills from Calvin.

1068
00:59:19,427 --> 00:59:20,427
Herbal medicine?

1069
00:59:26,327 --> 00:59:27,497
You really don't remember?

1070
00:59:29,067 --> 00:59:31,497
The one you asked Kyung Tae to get.

1071
00:59:33,807 --> 00:59:34,807
Kyung Tae?

1072
01:00:31,397 --> 01:00:34,367
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

1073
01:00:34,927 --> 01:00:36,537
It's been three years. What's the point now?

1074
01:00:36,597 --> 01:00:38,837
So that you can finally show some remorse and apologize.

1075
01:00:39,307 --> 01:00:40,407
What difference would that make?

1076
01:00:40,537 --> 01:00:42,107
So that was today...

1077
01:00:43,477 --> 01:00:44,477
Time flies.

1078
01:00:45,107 --> 01:00:46,777
You know what's really upsetting?

1079
01:00:47,647 --> 01:00:50,517
It's the fact that my husband has already forgotten all about it.

1080
01:00:51,717 --> 01:00:53,987
That brooch Mi Young lost...

1081
01:00:54,047 --> 01:00:56,087
I'd like to ask you something about this.

1082
01:00:56,557 --> 01:00:58,517
I thought you said you'd make Mi Young happy.

1083
01:00:58,887 --> 01:01:00,887
How would you know if she cries or laughs every day?

1084
01:01:01,257 --> 01:01:02,257
She cried yesterday...

1085
01:01:03,097 --> 01:01:04,097
because of you.
